:: Common {"position":"900,400","size":"100,100"}
The design team encounters the lack of key accessibility requirements; pressured by company to release by shareholders anyways against WCAG's wishes.

[[Ignore pressure, aim to implement accessibility options->Ethical Choice]]
[[Listen to the pressure, ignore implementing->Unethical Choice]]


:: EC1 {"position":"1200,100","size":"100,100"}
Shareholders are outrages while users are pleased.

[[outcome1]]


:: EC2 {"position":"1200,300","size":"100,100"}
The company is put back a step

[[The company decides to take a step back->Unethical Choice]]


:: Ethical Choice {"position":"1000,200","size":"100,100"}
The company owner agrees with the continuation of the tool's progress, but shareholders declare that they are tire of waiting for the product

[[The company prioritizes its users->EC1]]

[[The company listens to shareholders->EC2]]


:: Intro {"position":"700,400","size":"100,100"}
Start the Case Study

[[Common]]


:: UEC1 {"position":"1300,500","size":"100,100"}
The shareholders are dissatisfied. The users are satisfied.

[[outcome2]]


:: UEC2 {"position":"1300,700","size":"100,100"}
The shareholders AND the users are dissatisfied.

[[outcome3]]


:: Unethical Choice {"position":"1100,600","size":"100,100"}
Customer service is backed up by people complaining about the changes and wanting to downgrade; people reply by downloading the old version of the tool.

[[Roll everyone back to old version, continue work on new version->UEC1]]
[[Manage both old and new versions of tool->UEC2]]


:: outcome1 {"position":"1400,100","size":"100,100"}
The web-tool gets the accessibility it needs, but shareholders are slightly displeased. The company admits however that such a delay was necessary for the user-base.


:: outcome2 {"position":"1500,500","size":"100,100"}
The web-tool gets the accessibility it needs, but the company still need to take time to recover from operation costs for managing two versions of the tool.


:: outcome3 {"position":"1500,700","size":"100,100"}
The web-tool fails to get the accessibility tool and is met with backlash, thus damaing AllTogether's rep and losing them money.
